#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
News marks you can see, a plainer wires box, All on / All off, and a lighter
Cerulean download.

- News marks: a near-white dot with a dark rim inside a thin light ring, kept
  above every other layer (they had been drawn under the painted plate).
  Story titles in a mark's box are light text, not link purple.
- Wires box: the line of text beside the title is gone. Not offered as
  filters: Substance score, Direction, Why it was kept, Search feed, Search
  widened to (Time covers it). Country comes before Region. New: Source, the
  outlet that published each story.
- Layers: All on and All off, beside the caret.
- pipeline/cerulean/harvest_points.py: keeps only each record's id (a click
  reads the full record from Cerulean), pages by id so deep pages do not time
  out, and tiles only to the zooms the map shows the points at.

Needs patch_speed_row.py first.
Run from the repo root:  python3 patch_wires_marks.py
"""
